      "id": 1,
      "text": "Chisago City was founded in May 1857 by Anders Swenson, a Swedish immigrant from Småland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chisago_City%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Chisago City took its name from Chisago Lake, the nearby waterway in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chisago_City%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the railroad bypassed the original settlement in 1880, Chisago City relocated a mile north to sit beside the tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chisago_City%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city is between the twin lakes of Chisago Lake and Green Lake, and is part of the Chisago lakes region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chisago_City%2C_Minnesota"
    },
